      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rackerby takes its name from the local Racker family, early pioneers who helped settle the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/rackerby-114705"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Rackerby's history is tied to the Gold Rush era and the growth of Butte County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/rackerby-114705"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rackerby post office opened in 1892, moved to Butte County in 1930, and returned in 1934.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rackerby%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Rackerby sits 1,184 feet above sea level, about 24 miles north‑northeast of Marysville.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rackerby%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "As an unincorporated community, Rackerby has no municipal government and falls under county oversight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.wisdomlib.org/cities/rackerby-114705"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Today Rackerby remains a quiet, rural enclave surrounded by farmland and the Sierra Nevada foothills.",
